What is Medical Grade Polypropylene?
Medical grade polypropylene represents a specialized polymer formulation engineered explicitly for medical applications requiring direct contact with human tissues and fluids. Unlike standard PP, it undergoes rigorous purification processes and additives to achieve USP Class VI and ISO 10993-1 biocompatibility certifications. The material is distinguished by its:

Chemical inertness resisting drug interactions
Autoclavability (withstands 121°C sterilization)
Mechanical durability for device structural integrity

Two primary variants dominate the market: PP-H homopolymers (higher crystallinity) for rigid applications like surgical trays, and PP-R random copolymers (enhanced clarity) for IV components. Currently, medical infusion products account for 42% of consumption, while syringe applications represent another 28% of the market.

